"Questors come from the Distal Expansion, a technological civilization beyond Davrar."
"Questors built Davrar as a utopia experiment to test cultures; its population later surged."
"Davrar is a megastructure, a vast spinning cylinder the Questors built for a purpose."
"Questors once had the greater galaxy, but they are now cut off from it."
"A Questor's body on Davrar is truly tied to its mind through a link to Davrar."
"A Questor resurrects unless its link to Davrar is destroyed."
"Destroying a Questor's mana pool can kill it, as Ogarius's wispy pool dissipated."
"About 700,000 Questors exist, and only a few hundred are at the very top tier of power."
"Most Questors are about as strong as ordinary battlefield fighters."
"The elder Questors are the ancient founders; younger Questors came for entertainment."
"Some original Questors retreated from the game of Questors long ago."
"A Questor may choose to devote itself to Davrar for good."
"Questors could once call up a smart system for answers from outside Davrar."
"Young Questors lack hardship and misunderstand mortal life, money and even basic physics."
"Many Questors see mortals as livestock or as pieces on a board."
"Travel was granted to Questors later; before it they walked or used magic."
"Travel shows no mana or wizardry; it is a deeper effect of Davrar itself."
"Davrar forbids Questors from telling mortals some of their business."
"Most Questors would kill anyone who spreads the knowledge of fission."
"Questors hoard the Shields of Solemnance to limit the most horrible magics."
"A Conclave measure passes only if a majority of all Questors vote for it."
"Every Questor is granted access to the continent where a Conclave is held."
"A Questor who dies in a Conclave duel is exiled from that continent until it ends."
"The old Questor council of eighty-nine dissolved when its veto system broke."
"Questors fight regulated polite wars through mortals, adjudicated by Davrar."
"Later, Nathan suspects his antimagic might kill Questors for good."
"Years later, a Conclave's Charter lets mortals progress toward Questorhood through Quests."
"Eighty-one years later, Questors live under strict standards, policed by the grids."
